## Why This Is Asked

Assess practical planning for payment APIs, combining synchronous and asynchronous paths, contract testing, and real-world failure modes. Demonstrates handling of idempotency, webhook security, and end‑to‑end reliability.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys and duplicate request handling
- Webhook signature verification and replay protection
- OpenAPI contract testing and gateway simulation
- End-to-end flow with synchronous and asynchronous paths
- Retry/backoff policies and dead-letter queues

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: idempotent /charge test (high level)
const id = 'txn-123';
const r1 = post('/charge', {amount: 100}, {headers: {'Idempotency-Key': id}});
const r2 = post('/charge', {amount: 100}, {headers: {'Idempotency-Key': id}});
assert(r2.status === 200);
assert(r1.body.id === r2.body.id);
```

